    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>730ab5d3-bbac-5576-ff38-64635ac31551</Key>
      <Name>Concurrency</Name>
      <Alias>concurrency</Alias>
      <Definition>90cb2487-adcb-2ec5-c4a0-840175ba5424</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextBox</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[The version column: a whole number the engine increments on every update, or a SQL Server rowversion. Leave empty to compare a checksum of the row instead. A stale save returns a conflict.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>3</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="writes">Writes</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>48291e6c-8a51-26c2-87df-aa8929694d6a</Key>
      <Name>Connection</Name>
      <Alias>connection</Alias>
      <Definition>0bb63f2b-95ed-4a5a-81d4-5a7ddcd52751</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextBox</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description>The database to read and write: the separate AppBlocks database by default, a connection saved in Settings, or one registered in code. Select Umbraco's database only when the source needs CMS data. Credentials stay with the connection, and it can only do what its database account may.</Description>
      <SortOrder>1</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="definition">Definition</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>c020e8e9-5115-5e8b-9502-84de6e2ff4f4</Key>
      <Name>Key columns</Name>
      <Alias>keyColumns</Alias>
      <Definition>90cb2487-adcb-2ec5-c4a0-840175ba5424</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextBox</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[The columns that identify a row, separated by commas: the table's primary key or a unique key. Required when writes are allowed. A key of several columns appears in URLs as its values joined by |.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>3</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="definition">Definition</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>f448e697-3f4b-0247-2a5f-a3206ceb0062</Key>
      <Name>Read groups</Name>
      <Alias>readGroups</Alias>
      <Definition>b11c6fc7-5003-09af-5c9d-7dae42cd813b</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.MemberGroupPicker</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[Select at least one Member group for Specific groups access. Members in any read or write group may read. These groups also apply when Access is empty, preserving existing definitions. Public and Not public ignore read groups. Backoffice User groups do not count as Member groups.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>1</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="access">Access</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>fdbc1a5a-d332-cad9-89ff-ce1631851f23</Key>
      <Name>Row source</Name>
      <Alias>source</Alias>
      <Definition>64d2fba9-1cb2-490b-9de9-37211a072cf4</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextArea</Type>
      <Mandatory>true</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[A table name, such as ORDERS or dbo.ORDERS, or a SELECT without ORDER BY. With a SELECT, writes go to the table the key columns come from, and its other columns are read only. It may use :USER_, :PARAM. and :APP. bind variables; :APP.tenant, say, is a value the application's registered bind variable provider computes for the page and the person, so one source can serve a page copied per tenant.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>2</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="definition">Definition</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>ccc3c297-dd33-1e93-9c9b-b19864306562</Key>
      <Name>Write groups</Name>
      <Alias>writeGroups</Alias>
      <Definition>b11c6fc7-5003-09af-5c9d-7dae42cd813b</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.MemberGroupPicker</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[Member groups that may insert, update and delete. Empty: any signed-in reader. Public access never allows anonymous writes. Setting a group refuses backoffice Users, including Administrators; use a policy in code when they need access.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>2</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="access">Access</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>03c01bc0-4716-6ccf-d925-f334fe9b124a</Key>
      <Name>Mapping</Name>
      <Alias>mapping</Alias>
      <Definition>306b51cd-102b-ad7d-459c-be97ee8778e7</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextArea</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[Optional JSON from field alias to column, or to settings: { "client": "CUSTOMER", "orderDate": { "kind": "date" }, "region": { "choices": ["NORTH", "SOUTH"] } }. Settings are column, label, kind, choices, readOnly, required, maxLength, min and max. Every column is a field; one without an entry is named after it (ORDER_DATE becomes orderDate).]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>4</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="definition">Definition</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>cf024383-f802-82e3-74e3-5621c6493af4</Key>
      <Name>Row restriction</Name>
      <Alias>rowRestriction</Alias>
      <Definition>306b51cd-102b-ad7d-459c-be97ee8778e7</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextArea</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[Optional predicate added to every fetch and write, such as OWNER_SID = :USER_SID or REGION IN (:USER_GROUPS). It may use :USER_SID, :USER_NAME, :USER_KEY, :USER_EMAIL, :USER_GROUPS, :NOW and the :APP. values, never request parameters or field values. A write that would leave the restriction is refused.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>3</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="access">Access</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>123b5bbd-12c4-160a-3f98-7dd959a29b0b</Key>
      <Name>Insert defaults</Name>
      <Alias>insertDefaults</Alias>
      <Definition>306b51cd-102b-ad7d-459c-be97ee8778e7</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextArea</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[One per line, COLUMN = value: a bind variable (:NOW, :USER_NAME, :USER_SID, :PARAM.name, :FIELD.alias, :APP.name), a 'quoted' or plain literal, or NULL. A new record starts with these values, and an insert uses them for fields the form does not send.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>4</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="writes">Writes</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>1e459bb9-30ad-f759-e6e3-9678db20862c</Key>
      <Name>Audit columns</Name>
      <Alias>auditColumns</Alias>
      <Definition>306b51cd-102b-ad7d-459c-be97ee8778e7</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextArea</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[Optional, one per line: createdBy = COLUMN, createdAt = COLUMN, updatedBy = COLUMN, updatedAt = COLUMN. The engine writes the username and the server's local time; forms cannot change them.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>5</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="writes">Writes</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>74395163-846e-45b6-b88d-251e84f12be0</Key>
      <Name>Key sequences</Name>
      <Alias>keySequences</Alias>
      <Definition>306b51cd-102b-ad7d-459c-be97ee8778e7</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextArea</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[Optional Oracle JSON mapping, such as { "ORDER_ID": "ORDERS_SEQ" }. The engine validates each sequence in the database catalog and uses NEXTVAL for an omitted key. Useful for Oracle 11g; leave empty for identity columns.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>6</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="writes">Writes</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
    <GenericProperty>
      <Key>b5e2dd62-b6d6-6dcc-5ae3-7ff25ae561da</Key>
      <Name>Custom statements</Name>
      <Alias>customStatements</Alias>
      <Definition>306b51cd-102b-ad7d-459c-be97ee8778e7</Definition>
      <Type>Umbraco.TextArea</Type>
      <Mandatory>false</Mandatory>
      <Validation>
      </Validation>
      <Description><![CDATA[Advanced; off while empty. Sections that start with a line "-- insert", "-- update" or "-- delete" replace the generated statement and run whole, with bind variables such as :FIELD.customer bound as parameters. The engine still checks the version, the restriction and the policies.]]></Description>
      <SortOrder>0</SortOrder>
      <Tab Alias="advanced">Advanced</Tab>
      <Variations>Nothing</Variations>
      <MandatoryMessage>
      </MandatoryMessage>
      <ValidationRegExpMessage>
      </ValidationRegExpMessage>
      <LabelOnTop>false</LabelOnTop>
    </GenericProperty>
  </GenericProperties>
